---
import Base from '@cohorts/platform/layouts/Base.astro';
import { url } from '@cohorts/platform/url';
import { course } from '../course.config';
import TwoSteps from '../components/TwoSteps.astro';
import CourseMap from '@cohorts/platform/components/CourseMap.astro';
import { COURSE_MAP } from '../data/course-map';
---
<Base site={course} title={course.title}>
  <div class="home">
    <h1>{course.title}</h1>
    <p class="lead">{course.description}</p>
    <p><em>This course is in preparation.</em> Start with <a href={url('learn/')}>Learn</a>.</p>

    <h2>Two steps in translating, two things to check</h2>
    <p>Translating happens in two steps. First, find what the original author meant: that is <a href={url('glossary/#exegesis')}>exegesis</a>. Then say that same meaning in the new language: that is <a href={url('glossary/#re-expression')}>re-expression</a>.</p>
    <TwoSteps />
    <p>A translation check looks at both steps, one after the other:</p>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>The exegesis.</strong> Did the team understand the passage correctly? Where it can be read in more than one way, did they choose well?</li>
      <li><strong>The re-expression.</strong> Does the draft say that meaning clearly and naturally, with nothing added, left out or changed?</li>
    </ol>
    <p>This course is about the first: the exegesis a checker needs. Re-expression comes in only where it shows whether the meaning was understood, for example when the same meaning can be said in more than one way.</p>

    <CourseMap units={COURSE_MAP} heading="The course, level by level" intro="Exegesis works at every level, from a single word to a whole passage. Each level is one unit." />
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .home { max-width: 46rem; }
  .home .lead { font-size: 1.15rem; line-height: 1.5; }
  .home h2 { margin-top: 2rem; }
</style>
